  "prompt": "SQLite LENGTH counts text past a NUL after transpilation to DuckDB\n\nSQLite stops counting text at the first `\\0` (NUL character), while the translated DuckDB query counts the whole text. This can change length-based filters.\n\n```python\nimport sqlite3\nimport duckdb\nimport sqlglot\n\nquery = \"SELECT LENGTH('a' || CHAR(0) || 'b')\"\ngenerated = sqlglot.transpile(query, read=\"sqlite\", write=\"duckdb\")[0]\nprint(generated)  # SELECT LENGTH('a' || CHR(0) || 'b')\nprint(sqlite3.connect(\":memory:\").execute(query).fetchone())  # (1,)\nprint(duckdb.sql(generated).fetchone())                     # (3,)\n```\n\nReproduced on main `f59bcbcaa0ed549d61ed6d15f16f015cb2e9edc7`, SQLite 3.53.1 and DuckDB 2.0.0. SQLite's [LENGTH documentation](https://www.sqlite.org/lang_corefunc.html#length) specifies this behavior for text; BLOB length instead counts all bytes.\n\nAI assistance: OpenAI Codex assisted reproduction, implementation, and testing. The problem description was supplied by the contributor.",
